The problem is that it is necessary to ensure a minimum of trust in the  
exchange. I mean, if there is an "exchange shopkeeper" which is easily  
killable, in a server like NAO he will be always dead and then anybody can  
grab anything from the "backroom", even leading to players going for some  
"backroom-farming", waiting at the entrance and going in every 10 minutes  
to see what there is in it. This would certainly kill the whole stuff  
(since I, for  one, won't go for an exchange if I know that I'll risk  
giving something and getting nothing...)

And, indeed, the problem of dying/saving/... is also present. So here is a  
second try.

You'll need a new portal which ask you for a destination. The destination  
can be either "dungeon" (the shop in the dungeon where the portal is  
located, in Salsh'em, this would typically be the blackmarket) or any  
other (long enough) word/number/RSA key/... If the destination is a key  
and the corresponding closet is empty (no player in it), then you are  
taken there and can do what you want in it. So players wanting to trade  
goods must agree on a common secret word and then both of them (and only  
them) can enter the corresponding closet and do their trade there.

 From an implementation point of view, this is also rather easy (hum) :  
when a player leave a closet, save a bonefile of it. When a player enter a  
closet, load the bonefile (if it exists). Since the mechanism of bonefiles  
already exists for a limited sharing between game, and this protocol allow  
to reuse it, this should make thing easier to code. Of course, there must  
also be some routine to remove empty closet (to save disk space). Or,  
maybe better, allow only a certain number of entrance in a closet before  
deleting it (and also delete it if the file is too old on the computer,  
since it is deleted/recreated everytime someone goes in, that would ensure  
that nobody has used it for a long time).

Of course, the portal to the exchange room should located deep enough to  
prevent abuse but not too deep (after castle's wand, it becomes more or  
less useless). And there should be an associated conduct (you never  
entered the room of requirement). In Slash'em, the portal should  
definitely be in the blackmarket (thus, robbing Sam with the far too easy  
method of Xorn polyself will prevent you from going into the room of  
requirement again...)



